{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-141577","model_call":35,"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_660651092#2_1309335794"},"record":{"query":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_660651092#2_1309335794","op":"document"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_660651092#2_1309335794","document":"Paradise Falls | Disney Wiki | Fandom ... Paradise Falls Paradise Falls Paradise Falls Background information Feature films Inspiration Other information Location Inhabitants Visitors Status Role in the film Trivia  ... As a result, he is evicted from the house by court order and ordered to move to a retirement home. However, Carl comes up with a scheme to keep his childhood promise to Ellie: He turns his house into a makeshift airship, using thousands of helium balloons to lift it off its foundations. He then floats his house to Paradise Falls. Trivia Director Pete Docter and a select group of artists visited Canaima National Park in Venezuela to witness the tepuis firsthand, and to collect the sketches, photographs, and video that would later be used by art and technical directors as reference in creating their own \\\"Lost World.\\\" The name is likely based on Angel Falls, which is the highest waterfall in Venezuela. The Plateau of Paradise Falls, closely resembles the one from Sir Arthur Conan Doyle's The Lost World. In the English version of Up during the \\\"Married Life\\\" sequence in the part where Carl and Ellie make a savings jar, it is labeled \\\"Paradise Falls\\\". In the international versions of the film, the word itself was simply replaced by a picture of Paradise Falls itself to get over the language barrier. v - e - d Media Films:","ok":true,"op":"document"},"time":13},"model_calls":35,"document_judgments":21,"relevance_3":17,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
