{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-141577","model_call":52,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1822"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1822"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_624182566#4_1265307744","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1822","rank":7,"snippet":"\": \"Carl Fredricksen Carl Fredricksen Carl Fredricksen Background information Feature films Short films Television programs Video games Park attractions Animators Voice Inspiration Character information Full name Other names Occupation Home Likes Dislikes Partner (s) Pets Background Development Personality Appearances Up Dug's Special Mission George and A.J. Disney Parks Relationships Gallery Trivia References External links Languages: \" , \"segment\": \"As the years passed, the city grew around Carl's old house with construction as he refused to move. After confronting a construction worker over his broken <cover>mailbox, the court orders Carl to move into the Shady Oaks Retirement Home. </cover>Carl comes up with a scheme to keep his promise to Ellie: he uses his old professional supplies to create a makeshift airship, using 10,000 helium balloons, which lifts his house off its foundations. Russell, a young Wilderness Explorer (a fictional scouting organization), becomes an accidental passenger in an effort to earn his final merit badge for assisting the elderly. After surviving a thunderstorm, the house lands near a ravine facing Paradise Falls. Carl and Russell harness themselves to the still-buoyant house and begin to walk it around the ravine, hoping to ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_624182566#4_1265307744","rank":7,"relevance":3}]},"time":4},"model_calls":52,"document_judgments":24,"relevance_3":19,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-141577","model_call":52,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1822"},"model_calls":52,"document_judgments":24,"relevance_3":19,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-141577","model_call":52,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1822"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1822"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_1255972390#3_2581769714","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1822","rank":8,"snippet":"Spoilers Synopsis Contribute to This Page \" , \"segment\": \"When he meets Ellie, who also worships Muntz, they become close friends. However Charles Muntz falls into disgrace, accused of forging the skeleton of the monster of Paradise Falls. He travels in his blimp to South America to bring the monster back alive but is never seen again. Eventually Carl grows up and marries Ellie. They promise each other that they will travel together to Paradise Falls and build a house there. Many years later, Ellie dies and lonely Carl refuses to move from their home despite an offer from the owner of a construction company. When <cover>Carl accidentally hits a worker who damaged his mailbox, he is sentenced to move to a retirement home. </cover>However, he uses many balloons to float his house in order to travel to Paradise Falls. Adventure ensues. — Claudio Carvalho, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil Spoilers The synopsis below may give away important plot points.\" , \"start_char\": 1736.000000 , \"title\": \"Up (2009) - Plot Summary - IMDb\" , \"url\": \"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt1049413/plotsummary\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_1255972390#3_2581769714","rank":8,"relevance":3}]},"time":6},"model_calls":52,"document_judgments":24,"relevance_3":19,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
