{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-141577","model_call":63,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1828"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1828"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_1255972390#4_2581770904","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1828","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_1255972390#4_2581770904\" , \"end_char\": 3410.000000 , \"headings\": \" Up (2009) Plot Summaries Spoilers Synopsis Contribute to This Page \" , \"segment\": \"Many years later, Ellie dies and lonely Carl refuses to move from their home despite an offer from the owner of a construction company. When Carl accidentally hits a worker who <cover>damaged his mailbox, he is sentenced to move to a retirement home. </cover>However, he uses many balloons to float his house in order to travel to Paradise Falls. Adventure ensues. — Claudio Carvalho, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil Spoilers The synopsis below may give away important plot points. Synopsis Young Carl Fredricksen ( Jeremy Leary ), a quiet bespectacled boy wearing an old pilot's cap and goggles, watches a film reel in a theater depicting his hero Charles Muntz ( Christopher Plummer ), a famous explorer. The reporter speaks of Muntz's various accomplishments and discoveries before commenting that he was recently dishonored by scientists who believed his latest find, the large skeleton of a bird, was a hoax. Intent on proving them wrong, Muntz is ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_1255972390#4_2581770904","rank":2,"relevance":3}]},"time":5},"model_calls":63,"document_judgments":28,"relevance_3":19,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
